W34B37 OT ABI correction/reverification — 2026-08-23

Command:
  gdb -q -batch -ex 'set language c++' \
    -ex 'p sizeof(unsigned long)' -ex 'p sizeof(OT_TAG)' \
    -ex 'p sizeof(P_TAG)' -ex 'ptype OT_TAG' -ex 'ptype P_TAG' \
    pc_port/build_native/xeno-port

Authoritative production-binary debug-type result:
  sizeof(unsigned long) = 8
  sizeof(OT_TAG) = 8
  sizeof(P_TAG) = 8
  USE_EXTENDED_PRIM_POINTERS = 0

OT_TAG:
  unsigned int addr : 24;
  unsigned int len : 8;
  u_int _xeno_ot_pad;

P_TAG:
  unsigned int addr : 24;
  unsigned int len : 8;
  u_char pad0, pad1, pad2, code;

Source corroboration: pc_port/build_port.sh:244-254 explicitly documents
the port's eight-byte host-u_long OT padding. That existing fix was designed
for host-side u_long[] arrays. The world-map allocation is a retail raw
0x1000-byte guest buffer and its callbacks write four-byte OT words, so the
same padding cannot be applied to this world OT without an adapter decision.

Corrected diagnosis:
  retail stride = 4 bytes, 0x400 entries, 0x1000 bytes;
  production PsyCross stride = 8 bytes, 0x400 entries, 0x2000 bytes;
  retail DrawOTag input root+0xffc is 4-byte aligned but not 8-byte aligned;
  PsyCross-cleared links are low-24 host addresses, while world callback links
  are low-24 guest addresses such as 0x0009d310.

The class-(e) conclusion is unchanged. No production source was changed in
this re-verification; no backedge or second-frame iteration was implemented.
